A-09 cleartext fix, A/B on DN-ENG41 (Android 14, serial T3515NNFBC000055), 2026-11-02T03:15:43Z
Same device, same network, same intent:
  am start -a com.google.zxing.client.android.SEARCH_BOOK_CONTENTS -e ISBN 9780140328721 -e QUERY fox

This network cannot reach google.com at all (ping www.google.com: 100% loss; 223.5.5.5: 0% loss),
so the success path cannot be observed here. What the A/B shows is which failure happens.

--- BEFORE (http://www.google.com/books?...), build with SearchBookContentsActivity.kt at 787f24b51
11-02 11:15:21.661 29645 29674 W SearchBookContentsActivity: Error accessing book search
11-02 11:15:21.661 29645 29674 W SearchBookContentsActivity: java.io.IOException: Cleartext HTTP traffic to www.google.com not permitted
11-02 11:15:21.661 29645 29674 W SearchBookContentsActivity: 	at com.android.okhttp.HttpHandler$CleartextURLFilter.checkURLPermitted(HttpHandler.java:127)

--- AFTER (https://www.google.com/books?...), the fix
11-02 11:16:26.846 29783 29807 W SearchBookContentsActivity: Error accessing book search
11-02 11:16:26.846 29783 29807 W SearchBookContentsActivity: java.net.ConnectException: Failed to connect to www.google.com/104.244.42.197:443
11-02 11:16:26.846 29783 29807 W SearchBookContentsActivity: 	at com.android.okhttp.internal.io.RealConnection.connectSocket(RealConnection.java:147)

The request now leaves the app and opens a socket to port 443. Before, it never reached
the network: CleartextURLFilter rejected the URL inside okhttp. That is the whole of what
this fix claims, and it is what changed.

--- The endpoint itself, checked from the host, which can reach it
$ curl -sL -A 'ZXing (Android)' \
    'https://www.google.com/books?vid=isbn9780140328721&jscmd=SearchWithinVolume2&q=the'
{"number_of_results":3,"search_results":[{"page_id":"PA24","page_number":"24","snippet_text":
"... The smoke from the three guns floated upward in the night air . Boggis and Bunce and Bean ...

final URL after redirects: https://books.google.com.sg/books?vid=isbn...&redir_esc=y  (200)
first response: 301 -> books.google.<tld>, which is why HttpHelper now treats 301 like 302.

So the API still exists and still answers over https. What cannot be shown from here is
the app rendering those results, because this network does not reach google.com at all.

--- LocaleManager.isBookSearchUrl, widened to both schemes (device, fixed build)
https://books.google.com/books?id=sTDbBAAAQBAJ  -> title "Google Book Search"
http://books.google.com/books?id=sTDbBAAAQBAJ   -> title "Google Book Search"
9780140328721                                   -> title "Google Book Search: ISBN 9780140328721"

--- the same https URL on a build with LocaleManager.kt reverted to 787f24b51
https://books.google.com/books?id=sTDbBAAAQBAJ
  -> title "Google Book Search: ISBN https://books.google.com/books?id=sTDbBAAAQBAJ"

i.e. the old http-only test read a scanned https book URL as if it were an ISBN, so the
volume-id branch in SearchBookContentsActivity and BrowseBookListener was unreachable in
the field. Checked by reverting the one file and running the same intent, not reasoned.
